<title>Developing intuition about the derivative</title>

<description>
An intuitive exploration into the properties of the derivative, illustrated by interactive graphics.
</description>


<p><ref>Video</ref> | <ref>Applets</ref> | <ref>Transcript</ref>  </p>
<section name="vid_section"><title>Video</title>
<figure suppressFigureNameInCaption="true">
<video youtube="4H-vM5_kqPM" size="large" aspectRatio="16/9" name="v1" />
<caption>Developing intuition about the derivative</caption>
</figure>

<setup>
  <number name="timestamp1">200</number>
  <number name="timestamp2">270</number>
</setup>
  

<sideBySide margins="5%">
<div><p>Video credit achieved: <number displayDecimals="1">$v1RoundUp*100</number>%</p></div>

<div><updateValue type="number" target="$v1.time" newValue="$timestamp1" name="skipTo1">
  <label>Go to Key Moment 1</label>
</updateValue>
<updateValue type="text" triggerWith="$skipTo1" target="$v1.state" newValue="playing" name="playStamp1" />
</div>

<div><updateValue type="number" target="$v1.time" newValue="$timestamp2" name="skipTo2">
  <label>Go to Key Moment 2</label>
</updateValue>

<updateValue type="text" triggerWith="$skipTo2" target="$v1.state" newValue="playing" name="playStamp2" />
</div>
</sideBySide>


<number name="v1RoundUp" hide="true">
  <conditionalContent>
    <case condition="$v1.fractionWatched > 0.9">1</case>
    <else>$v1.fractionWatched</else>
  </conditionalContent>
</number>
  
<answer hide="true" name="v1Credit">
  <award credit="$v1RoundUp"><when>true</when></award>
</answer>

<callAction triggerWith="$v1" target="$v1Credit" actionName="submitAnswer" />


<problem><title>Video review questions</title>
<setup>
<number name="x">-3</number>
</setup>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>In the graph below, the $dragTangent.styleDescriptionWithNoun is tangent to the $f.styleDescriptionWithNoun, <m>f</m>. Click and drag the $dragPoint.styleDescriptionWithNoun to traverse the tangent lines of the function.</p>
<graph xmin="-12" xmax="12" ymin="-14" ymax="14" size="large">
  <function name="f" applyStyleToLabel="true">0.06x^3 + 0.4x^2 - 2x - 5
    <label><m>f</m></label>
  </function>
  <point name="dragPoint" styleNumber="2">($x,$$f($x))
    
      <constrainTo>$f</constrainTo>
    
  </point>
  <line name="dragTangent" styleNumber="2" slope="$$f_prime($x)" through="($x,$$f($x))" applyStyleToLabel="true">
    <label>slope <m>m = <math displayDecimals="2" extend="$dragTangent.slope" /></m></label>
  </line>
  <point name="localMax" styleNumber="5">$f.maxima
    <label><m>A</m></label>
  </point>
  <point name="localMin" styleNumber="5">$f.minima
    <label><m>B</m></label>
  </point>
  <function name="f_prime" hide="!$showDerivative" styleNumber="3"><derivative>$f</derivative></function>
  <line name="throughLocalMax" styleNumber="6" through="($f.maximumLocation1,0) ($f.maximumLocation1,1)" />
  <line name="throughLocalMin" styleNumber="6" through="($f.minimumLocation1,0) ($f.minimumLocation1,1)" />
</graph>
<booleanInput name="showDerivative">
  <label>Show <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m></label>
</booleanInput>


<p>Which statement below best describes the changes to the value of the derivative function <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m> between points <m>A</m> and <m>B</m>?
  <answer name="ans1">
    <choice>The value of the derivative function <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m>  stays a constant, negative value</choice>
    <choice>The value of the derivative function <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m>  starts at zero, and then becomes increasingly larger as it gets closer to point <m>B</m></choice>
    <choice>The value of the derivative function <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m>  starts at zero, and then becomes increasingly smaller as it gets closer to point <m>B</m></choice>
    <choice credit="1">The value of the derivative function <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m>  starts at zero, becomes increasingly negative until roughly around <m>x = -2</m>, and then becomes less and less negative. It is zero again at point <m>B</m></choice>
  </answer>
</p>

<hint hide="$ans1.numSubmissions &lt; 1 or $ans1.creditAchieved = 1 or $ans1.numSubmissions >= 2">
  <p>Remember, the value of the derivative function <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m> or <m>f'(x)</m> is equal to the slope of the tangent line to <m>f</m> at that point. See <ref to="$vid_section">Key moment 1</ref> in the video.</p>
  </hint>

  <hint hide="$ans1.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ans1.creditAchieved = 1">
    <p>What is happening to the slope of the tangent line to <m>f</m> as it traverses the function between points <m>A</m> and <m>B</m>? The value of the derivative function matches the slope of the tangent line at each point.</p>
  </hint>  
</exercise>

<exercise includeAutoNumber="true"><title />
<p>Fill in the blanks below to complete the sentence. (<ref to="$vid_section">Key moment 2</ref> may help.) </p>
<p>The <textInput name="userSlope" /> of the tangent line of <m>f</m> at any given <textInput name="user_xCoord" /> value is equal to the value of the <textInput name="userDerivative" /> function of <m>f</m> at that point.</p>

<p>Word bank:</p>
<sideBySide>  
  <ul>
    <li>function</li>
    <li>line</li>
    <li>output</li>
    <li>input</li>
</ul>
  <ul>
    <li>tangent</li>
    <li>slope</li>
    <li><m>y</m>-intercept</li>
    <li>derivative</li>
  </ul>
</sideBySide>

  
  <answer matchPartial="true" type="text" name="ans2">
    <award>
      <when>
        <textInput isResponse="true" extend="$userSlope" /> = slope and <textInput isResponse="true" extend="$user_xCoord" /> = input and <textInput isResponse="true" extend="$userDerivative" /> = derivative
      </when>
    </award>
  </answer>

<hint hide="$ans2.numSubmissions &lt; 2 or $ans2.creditAchieved = 1 or $ans2.numSubmissions >= 5">
  <p>Blank 1 hint: what is the word for <m>m</m>?, the <m>\frac{\text{rise}}{\text{run}}</m> of the tangent line?</p>
  <p>Blank 2 hint: a function is often referred to as an input-output machine. Which part of this name works better here?</p>
  <p>Blank 3 hint: What is the name for the function labeled <m>\frac{df}{dx}</m>, or equivalently, <m>f'(x)</m>?</p>
</hint>

  <hint hide="$ans2.numSubmissions &lt; 5 or $ans2.creditAchieved = 1">
    <p>The <alert>slope</alert> of the tangent line of <m>f</m> at any given <alert>input</alert> value is equal to the value of the <alert>derivative</alert> function of <m>f</m> at that point.</p>
  </hint> 

  <solution><p>The <alert>slope</alert> of the tangent line of <m>f</m> at any given <alert>input</alert> value is equal to the value of the <alert>derivative</alert> function of <m>f</m> at that point.</p></solution>
    
</exercise>
</problem>
</section>
